comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-28T14:00:13.238Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation note (2026-11-28): registerItemFields now judges each field against the declarations already admitted to the shared registration registry, plus the fields admitted earlier in the same call. It uses findConflictingItemFieldDeclaration in item-fields.ts, which reads names and types with the write path's own normalizeFieldName and normalizeFieldType, so activation and collectRegisteredFieldDefinitions can never disagree. The first declaration in activation order wins. A later one with another type is dropped with extension_item_field_type_conflict:<layer>:<package>:<field>:<type>:kept=<layer>:<package>:<type>, which package doctor and health carry as activation warnings, the same path the reserved-field warning takes. A same-type redeclaration is kept. A rolled-back package's declarations are truncated from the registry before later packages are judged (captureExtensionActivationRollback), so a failed package never shadows a later one. collectRegisteredFieldDefinitions keeps its typed refusal for hand-built registries, and the existing negative control still proves that refusal on create and update."
